  [$.sections[5].data] 210406-4 YAW DAMPER 1 IS PERODICALLY DROPPING OUT DURING FLIGHT - INVESTIGATE AND RECTIFY.
SUPPLIED FAULT HISTORY INDICATED THAT YD2 WAS ORIGINAL FAULT BUT AFTER SWAPPING FCC1A WITH FCC2A & FCC1B WITH FCC2B, THE YAW DAMPER FAULT TRANSFERRED TO YD1. ON ARRIVAL AT THE A/C, NO YAW DAMPER FAULT WAS EVIDENT. FCC1A & FCC1B YAW DAMPER TESTED IAW 22-11-10-802, NO FAULTS SHOWING. AS PER OPERATOR/BOMBARDIER REQUEST, FCC1A SWAPPED WITH FCCA1B IAW 22-12-10-000-801. FCC1A NOW S/N 4F1KNX. FCC1B S/N 4B6DY1. FCC1B REPLACED IAW AMM 22-12-10-000-801. FCC2A SWAPPED WITH FCC2B IAW 22-12-10-000-801. FCC2A NOW S/N 
  [$.sections[10].data] JTOTPILOT/FLIGHT DIRECTOR TRANSFERRED TO THE LEFT SIDE, ATTEMPTING TO SET A NEW PRESELECTED ALTITUDE RESULTS IN EITHER ERRATIC OR NO CHANGE - INVESTIGATE AND RECTIFY. BBD ADVICE REPLACE FCC. PN 822-0809-810.
